--TEST--
Core\Str::upper is Unicode-aware where strtoupper is byte-wise
--ORACLE-DIVERGES--
ADR 0009: `string` is guaranteed-valid UTF-8, so case mapping is the Unicode one; `strtoupper` leaves every non-ASCII byte alone.
--FILE--
<?mwl
echo Core\Str::upper("mwl"), "\n";
echo Core\Str::upper("straße"), "\n";
echo Core\Str::lower("ÉCOLE"), "\n";
--EXPECT--
MWL
STRASSE
école
